  <page>
    <title>Hirsutism</title>
    <id>101604</id>
    <revision>
      <id>41953769</id>
      <timestamp>2006-03-02T21:25:44Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <username>Arcadian</username>
        <id>104523</id>
      </contributor>
      <comment>clean up using [[Wikipedia:AutoWikiBrowser|AWB]]</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">{{DiseaseDisorder infobox |
  Name        = Hirsutism |
  ICD10       = L68.0 |
  ICD9        = {{ICD9|704.1}} |
}}
'''Hirsutism''' is the excessive growth of [[hair]], particularly on a woman's face, torso and limbs, and is generally caused by increased [[androgen]]s. It is a common sign of [[polycystic ovary syndrome]] in women. It can also be caused by a [[pituitary tumour]] or other serious medical conditions.

One method of evaluating hirsutism is the [[Ferriman-Gallwey score]] which gives a score based on the amount and location of hair growth on a woman.

Many people with unwanted hair seek methods of [[hair removal]] to control the appearance of hirsutism.

For men to be diagnosed with hirsutism, the amount of hair has to be exceptionally large. Often, such men (and on rare ocassions women)  are known as &quot;wolf people&quot;. During the nineteenth and early twentieth centuries, such people would exhibit in [[freak show]]s (e.g. [[Fedor Jeftichew]]).  

See also [[hypertrichosis]], a genetic condition that results in unusually thick body hair.

==External links==
*[http://www.hairchick.com/excess_hair/hirsutism.php Hairchick.com - Hirsutism] &lt;!-- despite the name of the page, it is actually informative and should remain linked --&gt;
*[http://www.hairfacts.com/index.html Hair removal facts for consumers.]
*[http://www.houstonmedcenter.com/articles/facial_hair_removal.php Facial Hair Removal for women]
*[http://www.darkskinlaser.com/forums Laser hair removal for darker skinned people]

[[Category:Human appearance]]
[[Category:Dermatology]]

