      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Crome's Broad''' is situated to the east of the [[River Ant]], north of [[How Hill]], within [[The Broads National Park]] in [[Norfolk, England|Norfolk]], [[England]].

It is named after [[John Crome]], the founder of the [[Norwich school]] of painters.

