'''Ulu&lt;u&gt;r&lt;/u&gt;u-Kata Tju&lt;u&gt;t&lt;/u&gt;a''' is a [[national park]] in the [[Northern Territory]] of [[Australia]], 1431 km (890 miles) south of [[Darwin, Northern Territory|Darwin]]. Its most important sites, after which it is named, are [[Uluru|Uluru / Ayers Rock]] and [[Kata Tjuta|Kata Tjuta / Mount Olga]]. Its major tourist resort is [[Yulara]].

''See also:'' [[Protected areas of the Northern Territory (Australia)]]
