[[Image:West_MacDonnell_National_Park.JPG|thumb|left|View along the West MacDonnell Ranges from the Larapinta Trail, near Glen Helen.]]
'''West MacDonnell''' is a national park in the [[Northern Territory]] ([[Australia]]), 1234 km south of [[Darwin, Northern Territory|Darwin]]. It extends along the [[MacDonnell Ranges]] west of [[Alice Springs, Northern Territory|Alice Springs]].

The popular extended walk, the [[Larapinta Trail]], runs East-West along the linear park, following the [[West MacDonnell Ranges]].  The park includes many tourist attractions along its 250 kilometre length including [[Ormiston Pound]], the [[Ellery Creek Bighole]], [[Simpson's Gap]], [[Mount Sonder]] and The [[Ochre Pits]].

