      <comment>I misapplied my own copyright tag</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">[[Fanfare]] from [[Igor Stravinsky]]'s ballet ''[[Petrushka]]''. Image made with [[Sibelius notation program|Sibelius]] and the [[GIMP]].

I'm not sure if this should be considered fair use or PD--if the music itself is PD, then I'm happy to release the image into the PD as well. As far as I know, however, ''Petrushka'' was not published until the 1940s (I may be wrong), in which case I guess we have to use it under fair use (which I would think we can, since its a very small excerpt of a much larger work, and one often used to demonstrate bitonality by writers, teachers and so on).

{{fairusein|Polytonality}}</text>
