  | coordinates = {{coor dms|35|00|47|S|138|39|21|E|type:landmark_region:AU}}
  | area = 8.4 km²
  | established = 1891
  | visitation_num = 
  | visitation_year = 
  | managing_authorities = [[Department for Environment and Heritage]]
  | official_site = [http://www.environment.sa.gov.au/parks/belair/ Belair National Park]
}}
[[Belair]] National Park is a national park in [[South Australia]] ([[Australia]]), 13 km south of [[Adelaide, Australia|Adelaide]]. It covers an 835ha area, and was the first National Park in South Australia. There are many areas of interest within the park, including Old Government House, the park Nursery, Playford Lake and the Adventure Playground. It has numerous tennis courts and ovals, and has walking trails, bike and horse-riding trails.

==See also==
* [[Protected areas of South Australia]]


{{SouthAustralia-geo-stub}}

{{National Parks of South Australia}}


[[Category:National parks of South Australia]]
[[Category:Parks in Adelaide]]

[[es:Parque Nacional Belair]]</text>
