'''Coorong''' is a national park in [[South Australia]] ([[Australia]]), 156 km southeast of [[Adelaide, Australia|Adelaide]].  The western edge of the Coorong starts at the [[Murray Mouth]] at [[Hindmarsh Island]] and the [[Sir Richard Peninsula]]. The park area includes the [[Coorong]] itself, and [[Younghusband Peninsula]] which separates the Coorong from [[Encounter Bay]] in the [[Southern Ocean]].

