'''Cradle Mountain-Lake St Clair''' is a national park in [[Tasmania]] ([[Australia]]), 165 km northwest of [[Hobart, Australia|Hobart]]. The park contains many walking trails, most famous of which is the [[Overland Track]]. Major features of the park are [[Lake St Clair, Tasmania|Lake St Clair]] and to the south, [[Cradle Mountain]]. This park is part of the [[Tasmanian Wilderness]] [[World Heritage Site]].

Wanting to avoid dangers of over-use, in 2005, the Tasmanian Parks &amp; Wildlife Service introduced a booking system &amp; fee for use of the Overland Track over peak periods.

Access from the south (Lake St. Clair) is usually from [[Derwent Bridge, Tasmania|Derwent Bridge]] on the [[Lyell Highway]]. Northern access (Cradle Valley) is usually via Sheffield or Wilmot.

==See also==
* [[Protected areas of Tasmania (Australia)]]

