[[nl:Savage River nationaal park]]
'''Savage River''' is a national park in [[Tasmania]] ([[Australia]]), 233 km northwest of [[Hobart, Australia|Hobart]]. It is the largest undisturbed area of [[temperate rainforest]] in Australia. 

The Savage River National Park was created as part of the [[Regional Forestry Agreement]] in 1999 to allow natural processes to continue undisturbed, consequently there are no recreational facilities or developments inside the reserve. The reserve is approximately 5% of the greater [[Tarkine]] area.

==See also==
* [[Protected areas of Tasmania (Australia)]]
* [[Tarkine]]
* [[Tasmanian temperate rain forests]]


