'''Southwest''' is a national park in [[Tasmania]] ([[Australia]]), 93 km west of [[Hobart, Australia|Hobart]].

It covers and area of over 6,000 km&amp;sup2; and is part of the [[Tasmanian Wilderness]] [[World_heritage|World Heritage area]].

The park is well known and its pristine wilderness and remoteness. The core of the park was created in the late 1960's as compensation for the flooding of [[Lake Pedder]].

Within the area there is only one road, to the [[hydro-electricity]] township of [[Strathgordon]] and one small air strip at [[Melaluca]].

[[Image:Southwest_np.jpg|left|frame|Cockle Creek, Southwest National Park]]
&lt;br clear=&quot;all&quot;&gt;
