  <page>
    <title>Degenerate distribution</title>
    <id>101843</id>
    <revision>
      <id>30935893</id>
      <timestamp>2005-12-11T16:02:06Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <username>Charles Matthews</username>
        <id>12978</id>
      </contributor>
      <minor />
      <comment>Reverted edits by [[Special:Contributions/81.164.99.135|81.164.99.135]] ([[User talk:81.164.99.135|talk]]) to last version by Michael Hardy</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">&lt;!-- EDITORS! Please see [[Wikipedia:WikiProject Probability#Standards]] for a discussion
of standards used for probability distribution articles such as this one. --&gt;

{{Probability distribution|
  name       =Degenerate|
  type       =mass|
  pdf_image  =[[Image:Degenerate_distribution_PMF.png|325px|Plot of the degenerate distribution PMF for k&lt;sub&gt;0&lt;/sub&gt;=0]]&lt;br /&gt;&lt;small&gt;PMF for k&lt;sub&gt;0&lt;/sub&gt;=0. The horizontal axis is the index ''k''. (Note that the function is only defined at integer values of k. The connecting lines do not indicate continuity.)&lt;/small&gt;|
  cdf_image  =[[Image:Degenerate_distribution_CDF.png|325px|Plot of the degenerate distribution CDF for k&lt;sub&gt;0&lt;/sub&gt;=0]]&lt;br /&gt;&lt;small&gt;CDF for k&lt;sub&gt;0&lt;/sub&gt;=0. The horizontal axis is the index ''k''. (Note that the function is only defined at integer values of k. The connecting lines do not indicate continuity.)&lt;/small&gt;|
  parameters =&lt;math&gt;k_0 \in (-\infty,\infty)\,&lt;/math&gt;|
  support    =&lt;math&gt;k=k_0\,&lt;/math&gt;|
  pdf        =&lt;math&gt;
    \begin{matrix}
    1 &amp; \mbox{for }k=k_0 \\0 &amp; \mbox{otherwise }
    \end{matrix}
    &lt;/math&gt;|
  cdf        =&lt;math&gt;
    \begin{matrix}
    0 &amp; \mbox{for }k&lt;k_0 \\1 &amp; \mbox{for }k&gt;k_0
    \end{matrix}
    &lt;/math&gt;|
  mean       =&lt;math&gt;k_0\,&lt;/math&gt;|
  median     =N/A|
  mode       =&lt;math&gt;k_0\,&lt;/math&gt;|
  variance   =&lt;math&gt;0\,&lt;/math&gt;|
  skewness   =&lt;math&gt;0\,&lt;/math&gt;|
  kurtosis   =&lt;math&gt;0\,&lt;/math&gt;|
  entropy    =&lt;math&gt;0\,&lt;/math&gt;|
  mgf        =&lt;math&gt;e^{k_0t}\,&lt;/math&gt;|
  char       =&lt;math&gt;e^{ik_0t}\,&lt;/math&gt;|
}}

In [[mathematics]], a '''degenerate distribution''' is the [[probability distribution]] of a discrete random variable that assigns all of the probability, i.e. probability 1, to a single number, a single point, or otherwise to just one outcome of a random experiment.  Examples are a two-headed coin, a die that always comes up six. This does not sound very [[randomness|random]], but it satisfies the definition of [[random variable]]. 

The degenerate distribution is localized at a point &lt;math&gt;k_0&lt;/math&gt; in the [[real line]]. The probability mass function is given by:

&lt;math&gt;f(k;k_0)=\left\{\begin{matrix} 1, &amp; \mbox{if }k=k_0 \\ 0, &amp; \mbox{if }k \ne k_0 \end{matrix}\right.&lt;/math&gt;

The [[cumulative distribution function]] of the degenerate distribution is then:

&lt;math&gt;F(k;k_0)=\left\{\begin{matrix} 1, &amp; \mbox{if }k\ge k_0 \\ 0, &amp; \mbox{if }k&lt;k_0 \end{matrix}\right.&lt;/math&gt;

There can be some ambiguity in the value of the cumulative distribution function at &lt;math&gt;k=k_0&lt;/math&gt;. In the above case the convention &lt;math&gt;F(k_0;k_0)=1&lt;/math&gt; has been chosen. 

==Status of its PDF==

As a discrete distribution, the degenerate distribution does not have a [[probability density function|density]]. 

The degenerate distribution of a continuous variable is described by the [[Dirac delta function]].

&lt;!--- This needs to go in the distribution article

But a serious theory awaited the invention of [[distribution|distributions]] by [[Laurent Schwartz]]. 

''NB: There is an unfortunate ambiguity in the meaning of the word distribution. The meaning given to it by Schwartz is not the meaning of the word distribution in [[probability theory]].''
 ---&gt;

[[Category:Discrete distributions]]
[[sl:izrojena porazdelitev]]</text>
