    <title>Dolly Madison</title>
    <id>101903</id>
    <revision>
      <id>39521069</id>
      <timestamp>2006-02-14T01:42:28Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <username>Rockhopper10r</username>
        <id>106460</id>
      </contributor>
      <text xml:space="preserve">:''This article is about the bakery brand. For the article on the U.S. First Lady (the wife of [[James Madison]]), see [[Dolley Madison]].''

'''Dolly Madison''' is a [[United States|U.S.]] bakery brand owned by [[Interstate Bakeries Corporation]], marketing pre-packaged baked [[snack foods]]. 

Its products include [[Zingers (Dolly Madison)|Zingers]] (finger-sized, creme-filled, iced [[cake]]s), [[Gems (Dolly Madison)|Gems]] (miniature [[doughnut]]s) and small [[pie]]s (actually fried [[turnover (food)|turnover]]s).

Dolly Madison snacks are probably best known for their long association with [[fictional character|characters]] from the ''[[Peanuts]]'' [[comic strip]]. [[Charlie Brown]] and his friends appeared on Dolly Madison packages and in [[television]] [[commercials]] in the [[1970s]] and [[1980s]]. The bakery was one of the sponsors of the ''Peanuts'' animated [[television special|specials]] during that period. Each pie flavor was sold with a different character on the label. For example, [[Peppermint Patty]] was on the [[peach]] pie label and [[Sally Brown]] was on [[coconut]] [[cream (food)|cream]] pie.

==External link==
[http://www.dollymadison.com/ Dolly Madison Web site ]

[[Category:Snack foods]]
[[Category:Interstate Bakeries brands]]</text>
    </revision>
