'''''The Emigrants''''' (''Utvandrarna'') is a [[1971]] [[film]] directed by [[Jan Troell]]. It tells the story of a [[Sweden|Swedish]] couple who emigrate to [[19th century]] [[United States|America]].  It stars [[Max von Sydow]], [[Liv Ullmann]], [[Eddie Axberg]], [[Sven-Olof Bern]], [[Aina Alfredsson]], [[Allan Edwall]], [[Monica Zetterlund]] and [[Pierre Lindstedt]].

The movie was adapted by [[Bengt Forslund]] and [[Jan Troell]] from the novels ''Utvandrarna'' and ''Invandrarna'' by [[Vilhelm Moberg]].

It was nominated for [[Academy Awards]] for [[Academy Award for Best Actress|Best Actress in a Leading Role]] (Liv Ullmann), [[Academy Award for Directing|Best Director]], [[Academy Award for Best Picture|Best Picture]] and [[Academy Award for Writing Adapted Screenplay|Best Writing, Screenplay Based on Material from Another Medium]].

The movie is in [[Swedish language|Swedish]].

