      <text xml:space="preserve">'''''A Touch of Class''''' is a [[1973]] romantic comedy film which tells the story of a couple having an affair, who find themselves falling in love.  It stars [[George Segal]], [[Glenda Jackson]], [[Paul Sorvino]] and [[K Callan]].

It was adapted by [[Melvin Frank]] and [[Jack Rose]] from the story ''She Loves Me, She Told Me So Last Night'' by [[Marvin Frank]].  It was directed by Melvin Frank.

The film won the [[Academy Award for Best Actress]] (Glenda Jackson) and was nominated for [[Academy Award for Original Music Score|Best Music, Original Dramatic Score]], [[Academy Award for Best Song|Best Music, Song]] (for [[George Barrie]] and [[Sammy Cahn]] for &quot;All That Love Went to Waste&quot;), [[Academy Award for Best Picture|Best Picture]] and [[Academy Award for Writing Original Screenplay|Best Writing, Story and Screenplay Based on Factual Material or Material Not Previously Published or Produced]].

